cabal-version:      2.2
name:               fire-number-calc
version:            0.1.0
synopsis:           Fire number and timeline math for early retirement planning
description:
  The arithmetic behind a fire number: the balance a withdrawal rate has
  to support, the gap between today's balance and that target, and the
  years of saving it takes to close the gap when the portfolio compounds
  at a fixed return.
  .
  The timeline function also prices a growing budget: a spending target
  that rises each year before retirement pushes the crossing point out,
  and the difference between the flat and growing timelines is the
  working-year cost of that growth.
  .
  Companion to Firenomics, which publishes the withdrawal-rate and
  sequence-of-returns math these functions follow. Four pure functions
  on Doubles, no dependencies beyond base.
license:            MIT
author:             Poket Dev
maintainer:         hello@poketdev.com
homepage:           https://firenomics.com
bug-reports:        https://github.com/scrapertweeter3-prog/fire-number-calc-hs/issues
copyright:          2026 Poket Dev LLC
category:           Math
build-type:         Simple
extra-doc-files:    README.md
                  , CHANGELOG.md

source-repository head
  type:     git
  location: https://github.com/scrapertweeter3-prog/fire-number-calc-hs

library
  exposed-modules:  FireNumber.Calc
  hs-source-dirs:   src
  build-depends:    base >=4 && <5
  default-language: Haskell2010
  ghc-options:      -Wall
